## Inside the macOS application

- Qt for Python: PySide6 6.12.0 and shiboken6 6.12.0
  (https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython/), "LGPL-3.0-only OR GPL-2.0-only OR
  GPL-3.0-only" as declared by the distribution. Used here under LGPL-3.0.
  The Qt libraries ship inside the bundle as separate dynamic libraries under
  Askbase.app/Contents/Frameworks and are not statically linked, so a user may
  replace them with a compatible build of their own. Qt modules that are
  GPL-only, Qt Virtual Keyboard among them, are dropped from the build on
  purpose; the exclusion list is in desktop/askbase.spec.
- sqlglot 30.23.0 (https://github.com/tobymao/sqlglot), MIT License.
- PyInstaller 6.22.3 bootloader (https://pyinstaller.org/), GPL-2.0-or-later
  with the bootloader exception, which gives unlimited permission to embed the
  compiled bootloader in a program under another licence.
- CPython (https://www.python.org/), Python Software Foundation License,
  embedded by PyInstaller.
- Fonts: Inter, Playfair Display and Space Grotesk, SIL Open Font License 1.1.
  The licence texts travel with the font files in
  desktop/askbase/fonts/licenses/ and are part of the bundle.


## Not included, installed by the person using Askbase

- Ollama (https://github.com/ollama/ollama), MIT License. Askbase reaches it
  over the loopback address. It is neither bundled nor installed by us.
- XiYanSQL-QwenCoder-7B-2504, Apache License 2.0
  (https://huggingface.co/XGenerationLab/XiYanSQL-QwenCoder-7B-2504), the
  model the application suggests by default. The quantisation used is
  mradermacher/XiYanSQL-QwenCoder-7B-2504-GGUF, also Apache License 2.0. Both
  derive from Qwen2.5-Coder, Apache License 2.0.
- Arctic-Text2SQL-R1-7B by Snowflake and Qwen2.5-Coder at 7B and 14B, each
  Apache License 2.0. They are measured in the model ranking and are not part
  of the application.


